I didn't set out to become a functional nutritionist. I became one because
conventional advice failed me. After years of my own digestive, hormonal, and
autoimmune struggles (and a lot of being told my labs were "normal"), I trained
as a **Functional Diagnostic Nutrition Practitioner** and paired it with formal
culinary training.

## How I work

I combine personalized functional lab testing, the kind that looks *underneath*
symptoms, with nutrition and lifestyle strategies that fit a real, busy life. No
100-ingredient protocols. No shame. Just root-cause work and food that tastes
good.

## Who I help

Women navigating perimenopause, weight-loss resistance, thyroid dysfunction, hair
loss, and stubborn gut issues, especially the ones who've been told everything
looks fine but know something isn't.
